===================================================
    
general SQL: HAVING with a subquery of USING INDEX ia(-), ib, ic(+): 2:2, 3:1     


===================================================
k    cnt    
2     2     
3     1     

Query plan:
iscan
    class: t? node[?]
    index: ib term[?] (covers)
    filtr: term[?]
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
(select min(t?.c) from t? t? where (t?.c> ?:? ) and (t?.d> ?:? ) using index t?.ia(-), t?.ic(+), t?.ib)
Query plan:
temp(order by)
    subplan: temp(group by)
                 subplan: sscan
                              class: t? node[?]
                              cost:  ? card ?
                 sort:  ? asc
                 cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select t?.c, count(*) from t? t? group by t?.c having (t?.c>(select min(t?.c) from t? t? where (t?.c> ?:? ) and (t?.d> ?:? ) using index t?.ia(-), t?.ic(+), t?.ib)) order by ?

